WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.136
-We're back with Michael Che.
Congrats on the special.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.037
I enjoyed it a great deal,
as I do with all your work.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.406
-Did you really watch it?
-I did.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:09.743
I watched the whole thing.
-I appreciate it. Thank you.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.143
Was it better than "Squid Game"?

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.880
-It was better than
"Squid Game."

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.783
I remember the whole time,
I was like,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.720
"Pound for pound, this is
better than 'Squid Game.'"

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.755
You shot it in Oakland.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.190
I know a lot of thought
goes into that,

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.190
where you're going to shoot it.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.692
Why did you pick Oakland?

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:30.497
-Well, I picked Oakland because
Oakland's a lot like New York,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.132
but it's on the West Coast.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.800
-Yeah.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.935
-I kind of just wanted
to pick a city

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.737
that I thought was gonna

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:42.374
take good cares
of the COVID precautions.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:43.876
You know what I mean?

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:47.247
Like, I didn't want to do it
in Alabama.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.482
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.217
A guy liking his hand
and shaking mine.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.818
I'm like, eughhh.

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:55.621
-You're right.
That was a good, safe choice.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:57.723
-Yeah, Oakland was kind of like,
you know,

00:00:57.723 --> 00:00:58.858
it's a hip, together city.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.394
I figure they probably
would be fine with

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.762
wearing masks
and getting the vaccine.

00:01:03.762 --> 00:01:07.934
-Is it okay, can I talk about
something in the special?

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.236
I don't want to like,
burn material, but...

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.938
-Please. It's longer
than "Squid Game."

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.239
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.742
-I did enjoy a great deal
that you admitted to not --

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.945
there was a moment where you
changed your mind about masks,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.146
which was right around,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.681
people told you
you could stop wearing them.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.782
-That's true.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.617
Last spring, everybody was like,

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.319
"Oh, we're gonna have
a maskless summer."

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.488
And I was like,
"I want my mask now."

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:31.758
'Cause that is not
what you want to hear.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.227
It's like when a woman says
"You don't need a condom."

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.629
Like, "I need two condoms."

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.865
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.199
I wasn't even
thinking about a condom

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:44.070
before you said that nasty...

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.073
You need to be more careful,
lady.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.942
-You know, we have Adam Schiff
is coming up next.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.844
I'm gonna ask him some questions
about January 6th.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:54.146
You also mentioned January 6th
in your special.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:56.049
That was a bit eye-opening
for you.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.818
-It was.
I really, thoroughly enjoyed it.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:01.354
[ Laughter ]
-I did.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.489
You guys got to understand,
for a black guy, like,

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.424
we don't know all the rules,

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.760
so when I see a bunch of
white people storm the Capitol,

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.563
I'm like, "You can do that?"

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.732
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.667
Think of the possibilities!

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.001
This whole time, I thought

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:18.504
we had to loot at Louis Vuitton
or the Gucci store.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:23.709
Nope. We could steal
the Constitution.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.378
Wait till that
next rally happens.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:31.484
Next protest that black people
have, ooh, it's gonna be fun.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.387
-I guess, because
Thanksgiving's coming up,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.621
you mentioned your mom.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.756
I know that she's hesitant
to get the vaccine.

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:39.125
Has she changed her mind?

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.960
-Uh, I don't know.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.361
I'm not allowed to say, maybe.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.997
Maybe she did.
Maybe she didn't.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.064
-Okay.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.399
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.434
-I'm trying to get that pie,
man.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.668
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:52.038
But you explained --
-She was skeptical.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.840
She was skeptical to get it
initially,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.042
because her neighbor got it
and then died,

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.578
like, two days later.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:03.282
Yeah, he got hit by a truck,
and she...

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.783
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.420
She thinks the vaccine's
unlucky.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.455
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.290
There's a lot of people
in my family who, like,

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.092
won't get the vaccine.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.161
I got an aunt,
she won't get it either.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.764
She got one foot.
She's afraid to get the vaccine.

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:22.235
She lost her foot
drinking Pepsi for breakfast.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:25.838
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.941
But she don't know
what's in the vaccine,

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:31.444
so she's doing her own research.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.846
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.180
You know.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:41.454
-But you do admit that there is
a reason for skepticism.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.922
-Of course.
-That people who are --

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.056
-I was skeptical.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.525
Look, I'm vaccinated
and I was skeptical.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:50.196
-Yeah.
-Because it was free.

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:55.034
I was like, "Free medicine?
In America? Since when?"

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.436
I didn't trust it.
They was like, "trust science."

00:03:57.436 --> 00:04:00.139
I was like,
"Well, I trust history."

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.908
And history says,
if this thing worked,

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.710
you'd be charging us for it.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.345
It the vaccine was $3,000,

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.114
I would have been like,
"Yeah, that sounds about right."

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:10.850
That's pretty American.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.851
You know what's
the funniest thing about

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:14.821
watching a stand-up special,
having done one,

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.889
is I think the structure of
a special is really important.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.624
I think that's what
makes it special, often,

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:22.862
and the end of yours
talks a lot about mental health,

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.598
especially mental health
in the black community

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.466
and just how much it's changed
and how awareness

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.969
has actually been
moving in the right direction.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:34.640
-Yeah,
I call it "sarcastic optimism."

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.010
You guys know what that is?
Sarcastic optimism?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.380
It's optimism, but sarcastic.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.415
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:44.617
-It tracks.
-Yeah.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.318
Because it becomes, like,
this big conversation,

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:47.720
"Oh, black mental health."

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.557
I'm like, really? You just
found out we had brains, too?

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.893
Why wouldn't we have
mental health issues?

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.929
It's just things that
you never really think of

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.131
until you actually think of.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:02.035
These aren't black issues,
these are human issues.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.769
-Yeah, and it's really nice.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:06.439
You do a very nice job --

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.507
again, I don't want to
give anything away,

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:11.610
but it ends very funny,
but it must be --

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.680
do you like dealing with
an issue and finding humor in

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.014
something that maybe people
would have thought

00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:18.317
"Oh, that's not gonna be
fun to do onstage."

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:20.352
Because it's deeply funny,
but it will resonate with me.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:21.353
It's gonna stay with me.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.055
-Yeah, I always like that.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:25.291
I always like our audience
coming to the show

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.027
and walking away like,
"Hey, I never thought of that."

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:32.031
Even if it's a bad joke.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.398
'Cause some of them
are bad jokes.

00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:34.466
I'm not gonna lie to you.

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:36.836
No one's perfect.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.471
But I always like that.

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:43.843
I always like looking at things
in a weird way

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:47.379
and going dark, going bright,
whatever.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:48.548
-It's a nice balance.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:50.049
-This is the most painful
thing in the world,

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.483
to talk about your comedy.

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:53.052
You feel like the biggest fraud.
-I will say,

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:56.121
it's really hard to
talk about a special,

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:58.624
'cause really, the answer
is like, just watch it.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.559
So I apologize.
-That's perfect!

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.461
Just watch it!
-Just watch it.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:05.331
I promise, you won't regret it.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.899
-You won't regret it.
Michael Che.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.700
"Shame the Devil"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.702
It's fantastic.

